{"ts": "2026-10-24T13:37:12.057240+00:00", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "temperature": 0.3, "arm": "dense", "task_id": "T01", "lang": "en", "category": "decision", "rep": 0, "system_tokens_approx": 304, "ok": true, "text": "`pg_trgm`.\n\nAt 200k rows the whole trigram index fits in memory and queries stay in the low milliseconds, so Elasticsearch buys you nothing for this size and costs you a second datastore, a sync pipeline, and a consistency problem. The one thing that would flip this is needing relevance ranking tuned per-field or fuzzy search across tens of millions of rows.\n\n```sql\nCREATE EXTENSION pg_trgm;\nCREATE INDEX idx_search_trgm ON your_table USING gin (searchable_col gin_trgm_ops);\n```\n\nQuery with `searchable_col % 'typo'` or `similarity(searchable_col, 'typo') > 0.3`. Note `%` uses `pg_trgm.similarity_threshold` (default 0.3); set it per session if you need a different cutoff.", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 340, "completion_tokens": 343, "total_tokens": 683, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 170}, "cost": 0, "opencode": {"billing_source": "go", "list_cost": 0.0002568, "allowance": 0.0001926, "tokens": {"input": 340, "output": 343, "reasoning": 170, "cache_read": 0, "cache_write_5m": 0, "cache_write_1h": 0}}}, "latency_ms": 3824, "attempt": 1}
